RisuAI - Curly Braced Syntaxes (CBS) Reference
Source: https://kwaroran.github.io/docs/syntax/cbs/

OVERVIEW
Curly braced syntaxes (e.g. {{user}}) insert special values into text. They
can be used in almost any text field in the client: chat messages, character
descriptions, lorebook entries, etc.

• They are replaced with actual values when a message is sent or when text
is displayed in the client.
• They can be nested and combined, e.g.
{{calc::{{getvar::a}}+{{getvar::b}}}}
• They are case-insensitive: {{user}}, {{User}}, {{USER}} are identical.
• Parameters are separated by "::" (two colons).
• Some syntaxes need arrays as parameters. Create one with
{{array::A::B::C...}}
• Block syntaxes start with {{#NAME A}} and end with {{/NAME}} (or simply
{{/}}). They start with "#" and can be nested. Indentation and whitespace
inside a block are trimmed, except for syntaxes like {{#if-pure A}},
which keep them.

Notation: "Alias" lists alternative names for the same syntax.

1. DATA SYNTAXES

───

{{user}}
The persona's name.

{{char}}
The character's name. In a group chat: if the speaker is the user, the
group chat name; if the speaker is a character, that speaker's name.

{{description}} Alias: {{char_desc}}
The character's description.

{{example_dialogue}} Alias: {{example_message}}
Array of the character's example dialogue.

{{persona}} Alias: {{user_persona}}
The persona's description.

{{lorebook}} Alias: {{world_info}}
Array of lorebook entries.

{{history}} Alias: {{messages}}
Array of messages in the current chat.

{{chat_index}}
Index of the message in the chat. Starts at 0, except the first message
which is -1. Outside chat context: -1.

{{model}}
Current model ID of the client.

{{axmodel}}
Current auxiliary model ID of the client.

{{role}}
Role of the current message sender. Outside chat context: the string
"role".

{{maxprompt}}
The client's maximum tokens setting.

{{lastmessage}}
The last message in the chat log.

{{lastmessageid}} Alias: {{lastmessageindex}}
Index of the last message in the chat log.

{{previous_char_chat}} Alias: {{lastcharmessage}}
The character's last message in the chat log.

{{previous_user_chat}} Alias: {{lastusermessage}}
The user's last message in the chat log.

{{previous_chat_log::A}}
The chat message at index A. If it does not exist: "Out of range".

{{first_msg_index}}
Index of the first message in the chat log.

{{screen_width}} / {{screen_height}}
Screen width / height in pixels.

{{user_history}}
Array of the user's messages in the chat log.

{{char_history}}
Array of the character's messages in the chat log.

2. TIME SYNTAXES

───

{{time}}
Current time as HH:MM:SS in the client's timezone.

{{time::A}} Alias: {{datetimeformat:A}}, {{date::A}}
Current time formatted by A, in the client's timezone. Format tokens:
YYYY year YY year (2 digits)
MM month DD day
DDDD day count of year
HH hour (24-hour) hh hour (12-hour)
mm minute ss second
A AM/PM X unix timestamp
x unix timestamp in milliseconds
Example: {{time::YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss}} -> 2024-12-31 23:59:59

{{time::A::B}} Alias: {{datetimeformat::A::B}}, {{date::A::B}}
Same as {{time::A}}, but uses unix timestamp B instead of the current
time.

{{date}}
Current date as YYYY-MM-DD in the client's timezone.

{{isotime}}
Current time as HH:MM:SS in UTC.

{{isodate}}
Current date as YYYY-MM-DD in UTC.

{{message_time}}
Time the message was sent (format depends on browser/OS settings).
- Non-chat context or first message: "[Cannot get time]"
- Message sent before this syntax existed: "[Cannot get time, message
was sent in older version]"

{{message_date}}
Date the message was sent (format depends on browser/OS settings).
Same fallback strings as {{message_time}}.

{{message_idle_duration}}
Time between the user's previous message and the one before it
(HH:MM:SS).
- Non-chat context or first message: "[Cannot get time]"
- Older messages: "[Cannot get time, message was sent in older version]"
- No previous messages: "[No user message found]"

{{idle_duration}}
Time between the user's previous message and now (HH:MM:SS).

{{message_unixtime_array}}
Array of unix timestamps of the chat log.

3. EMOTION / ASSET SYNTAXES

───

(A = name of the asset/emotion of the current character)

{{asset::A}}
Element whose source is the additional asset named A. The element type
is chosen automatically from the asset type.

{{emotion::A}}
Image element using the emotion image named A.

{{audio::A}}
Audio element using the additional asset A.

{{bg::A}}
Background image element using the additional asset A.

{{video::A}}
Video element using the additional asset A.
{{video-img::A}}
Like {{video::A}}, but displayed like an image element.

{{raw::A}}
The raw path data of the additional asset A.

{{image::A}}
Image element using the additional asset A.

{{img::A}}
Unstyled image element using the additional asset A.

{{assetlist}}
Array of names of the character's additional assets.

{{emotionlist}}
Array of names of the character's emotion images.

{{source::A}}
Path of an icon. A = "char" -> character's icon; A = "user" -> user's
icon.

4. MATH SYNTAXES

───

{{? A}} Alias: {{calc::A}}
Evaluates the expression A, e.g. {{? 5+3}} -> 8. Other syntaxes can be
nested inside. Numeric and boolean values only (use {{equal::A::B}}
for strings).

Operators:
A+B A-B A*B A/B add, subtract, multiply, divide
A%B remainder
A^B A to the power of B
A||B A&&B !A or, and, not
A==B A!=B equal, not equal
A>B A>=B A<B A<=B comparisons
$<name> value of chat variable <name> (alphanumeric
and underscore only)
Operator aliases: | for ||, & for &&, = for ==, ≤ for <=, ≥ for >=
Booleans: 1 = true, 0 = false.
{{equal::A::B}}
1 if A equals B, else 0. Works for any value type.

{{not_equal::A::B}} Alias: {{notequal::A::B}}
1 if A does not equal B, else 0. Works for any value type.

{{remaind::A::B}}
Remainder of A divided by B.

{{greater::A::B}}
1 if A > B, else 0.

{{greater_equal::A::B}} Alias: {{greaterequal::A::B}}
1 if A >= B, else 0.

{{less::A::B}}
1 if A < B, else 0.

{{less_equal::A::B}} Alias: {{lessequal::A::B}}
1 if A <= B, else 0.
{{and::A::B}}
1 if both A and B are 1, else 0.

{{or::A::B}}
1 if A or B is 1, else 0.

{{not::A}}
1 if A is 0, else 0.

{{pow::A::B}}
A raised to the power of B.

{{floor::A}} Largest integer <= A.
{{ceil::A}} Smallest integer >= A.
{{abs::A}} Absolute value of A.
{{round::A}} A rounded to the nearest integer.

{{min::A::B::C...}}
{{max::A::B::C...}}
{{sum::A::B::C...}}
{{average::A::B::C...}}
Smallest / largest / sum / average of the parameters. With only one
parameter, A is treated as an array of values.

{{fix_number::A::B}}
A with the number of decimal places fixed to B.

5. STRING SYNTAXES

───

{{startswith::A::B}} 1 if A starts with B, else 0.
{{endswith::A::B}} 1 if A ends with B, else 0.
{{contains::A::B}} 1 if A contains B, else 0.
{{lower::A}} A in lowercase.
{{upper::A}} A in uppercase.
{{capitalize::A}} A with the first letter capitalized.
{{trim::A}} A with leading/trailing whitespace removed.
{{unicode_encode::A}} A encoded to unicode (result is a number).
{{unicode_decode::A}} A decoded from unicode (input is a number).

6. CONDITIONAL SYNTAXES

───

{{prefill_supported}}
1 if the model supports prefilling, else 0.

{{jbtoggled}}
1 if the jailbreak toggle is enabled, else 0.

{{isfirstmsg}}
1 if the message is the first message in the chat, else 0.

{{all::A::B::C...}}
1 if all parameters are 1, else 0. With one parameter, A is treated as
an array of values.

{{any::A::B::C...}}
1 if any parameter is 1, else 0. With one parameter, A is treated as an
array of values.

{{module_enabled::A}}
1 if the module with namespace A is enabled, else 0.

7. VARIABLE SYNTAXES

───

{{getvar::A}}
Value of chat variable A, or "null" if undefined.

{{setvar::A::B}}
Sets chat variable A to B; outputs an empty string. Only works in chat
context and not in the first message. A trigger script is recommended
instead when possible.

{{addvar::A::B}}
Increments chat variable A by B; outputs an empty string. (If A is 5,
{{addvar::A::3}} makes it 8.) Only works in chat context and not in the
first message.

{{settempvar::A::B}}
Sets temporary variable A to B; outputs an empty string. Only works in
chat context and not in the first message. Temporary variables exist
only in the current context and are not saved when the chat is closed,
but they are performance-optimized.

{{gettempvar::A}}
Value of temporary variable A, or "null" if undefined.

{{getglobalvar::A}}
Value of global variable A, or "null" if undefined.

8. ARRAY SYNTAXES

───

{{array::A::B::C...}}
Creates an array from the parameters. Arrays currently use "§" as the
separator, which may change, so use this syntax rather than "§"
directly.

{{array_length::A}} Alias: {{arraylength::A}}
Length of array A (does not work with strings).

{{array_element::A::B}}
Element of array A at index B (0-based). Out of range -> "null".
Negative index counts from the end.

{{array_push::A::B}}
Array A with element B pushed to the end.

{{array_pop::A}}
Array A with the last element removed.

{{array_shift::A}}
Array A with the first element removed.

{{array_splice::A::B::C::D...}}
Array A with C, D, ... inserted at index B.

{{array_assert::A::B::C}}
Array A with element C inserted at index B.

{{split::A::B}}
Array of the strings in A separated by B.

{{join::A::B}}
String made by joining the elements of array A with B.

{{filter::A::B}}
Array A filtered by option B:
nonempty - remove empty strings
unique - remove duplicate elements
all - both nonempty and unique

9. DICTIONARY SYNTAXES

───

{{dict::A=B::C=D...}} Alias: {{object::...}}, {{o::...}}, {{d::...}}
Dictionary with keys A, C, ... and values B, D, ...

{{dict_element::A::B}} Alias: {{object_element::A::B}}
Value of key B in dictionary A.

{{dict_assert::A::B::C}} Alias: {{object_assert::A::B::C}}
Dictionary A with key B and value C inserted.

10. UTILITY SYNTAXES

───

{{slot}}
In a prompt template, pipeline, or translator prompt: replaced by the
original slot content. Otherwise not replaced.

{{slot::A}}
Inside a {{#each C D}} block, if D equals A, replaced by the current
array element. Otherwise not replaced.

{{position::A}}
In a prompt template: replaced by the lorebooks using position
"pt_<A>" (e.g. pt_personality). Empty string if none exist. Otherwise
not replaced.

{{random::A::B...}} Alias: {{random:A,B...}}
A random value from the parameters. With no parameters: a random number
between 0 and 1.

{{pick::A::B...}} Alias: {{pick:A,B...}}
Like {{random}}, but seeded per message so the result is consistent.
Does not work with no parameters.

{{roll::A}} Alias: {{roll:A}}
Random number from 1 to A. If A starts with "d", the "d" is ignored.

{{rollp::A}} Alias: {{rollp:A}}
Like {{roll}}, but seeded per message so the result is consistent.

{{spread::A}}
Joins the elements of array A with "::" so arrays can feed
multi-parameter syntaxes. Example:
{{random::{{spread::{{array::chicken::pizza::hamburger}}}}}}
acts the same as {{random::chicken::pizza::hamburger}}.

{{replace::A::B::C}}
A with all occurrences of B replaced by C.

{{range::A}}
Array of numbers from 0 to A-1.

{{length::A}}
Length of A (does not work with arrays).

{{none}} Alias: {{blank}}
An empty string. Useful for removing default text. If used in the first
message, the first message behaves as if it does not exist.

{{br}} Alias: {{newline}}
A line break.

{{tonumber::A}}
Trims all non-numeric characters except ".". The result is not
guaranteed to be a valid number.

{{return::A}}
The whole message is replaced with A and the rest is ignored.

{{func::A::B::C...}}
Result of calling function A with arguments B, C, ...

{{arg::A}}
The argument at index A of the function when called via
{{func::A::B::C...}}.

11. BLOCK SYNTAXES

───

{{#if A}} ... {{/if}}
Content is kept if A is 1, otherwise replaced by an empty string.
Example:
{{#if {{equal::1::1}}}}
Hello Alice!
{{/if}}

{{#if-pure A}} ... {{/if-pure}}
Same as {{#if A}}, but keeps the content's indentation and whitespace.

{{#each A B}} ... {{/each}}
Repeats the content for each element of array A; the current element is
available as B (use {{slot::B}}). Example:
{{#each {{array::chicken::pizza::hamburger}} item}}
{{slot::item}}
{{/each}}
Result: chickenpizzahamburger

{{#func A}} ... {{/func}}
Defines/uses function A; it can be called with {{func::A::B::C...}}.

{{#pure_display}} ... {{/pure_display}}
Content shown without any formatting. Useful for displaying raw text.
